# N aerosol species in the radiation, instead of one. CLIM-39.
#
# ITS DIFFUSE-BEAM LINES ARE SUPERSEDED AND THE SUBTREE IS RIGHT. The diff below
# rewrites zaertf1s, zaerd1s, zaert1s and zaerr1s for the per-cell arrays and
# preserves an upstream transcription error while doing so: zaerd1s was built
# from the direct-beam zaertf1, and zaert1s and zaerr1s divided by the
# direct-beam zaerd1, so the diffuse transmission and reflection came out
# bit-identical to the direct ones and the factor-of-2 diffusivity the scattered
# stream carries was absent. This patch's new conservative-scattering branch
# then set zaert1s = zaert1 and zaerr1s = zaerr1 outright, which made the defect
# read as deliberate. world-sv7 repaired both bands and both branches in the
# subtree; nothing else in this patch is affected, and the multi-species work it
# is about is unchanged.
#
# WHAT THIS IS FOR. aeolian/ produces three aerosol species and
# analysis/error_budget.json prices all three: mineral dust at +0.34 to +0.61
# W/m2, sea salt at -0.16 to -0.89, volcanic sulfate at -0.013 to -0.032. None
# of them was in the radiation, and the interface would not take more than one,
# so the species of comparable magnitude to dust and OPPOSITE sign had no route
# in at all. aeolian/notes/multi-species-aerosol.md is the design.
#
# WHY ONE SLOT WAS THE LIMIT. radmod declared aeroqs(8,1) and derived ssa1,
# ssa2, bscat1, bscat2, qex1 and qex2 from it as SCALARS: one set of optical
# properties for the whole planet. Only the optical depth varied in space. Dust
# absorbs and sea salt's single-scattering albedo is 1 to within 1e-5, so no one
# value describes both, and dust transports over ocean, so the two are
# co-located rather than separable by geography.
#
# BASE.
#
#   radmod.f90   9b45ec44a86ccc2eba429cd576ee5ea202acbc15d1bbfcf623a50690bc6cb86f
#   surfmod.f90  545eb13ee85dd8bf6bddd0fc1983c5fd8ded1e412d2da622b2478bb6b4145a91
#
# RESIDENT, and every executable must be rebuilt after it lands (CLAUDE.md rule
# 4). It is a no-op at ndustrad = 0 with l_aerorad = 0, which is the default.
#
# WHAT IT ADDS.
#
#  1. NAERSP, a plain parameter, the number of radiative species carried at
#     once. NOT pumamod's NAERO, which is how many TRANSPORTED tracers aerocore
#     carries; the two counts are independent and conflating them is why the
#     first build failed. Set to 4: dust, sea salt, sulfate, and one spare for
#     the carbonaceous aerosol CLIM-29 is waiting on a biosphere run for.
#
#  2. The optical constants become per-species arrays, and the aerofile gains
#     one COLUMN per species. That axis already existed: readdat's `ndim`
#     argument is the species count and it was passed as 1, so the file format
#     extends rather than changes and an existing single-species aerofile stays
#     valid.
#
#  3. ndustrad becomes a COUNT of prescribed species rather than a switch. 0 and
#     1 mean exactly what they meant before. Species s reads surface code
#     1810+s; 1811 keeps the name ddustcol so .sra files already on disk stay
#     readable. dustsc, dusthsc and dustqlw become arrays, and a namelist that
#     assigns one value still sets element 1, so existing namelists are
#     unchanged in effect.
#
#  4. Per-species scale heights in dustprof, because a sea salt layer sits in
#     the boundary layer and dust does not. One shared height would put the
#     second species at the first one's while the column total still looked
#     right, so dustprof's column-conservation report is now PER SPECIES.
#
#  5. The external mixture in swr, which is the whole cost. tau adds; the
#     single-scattering albedo is the extinction-weighted mean and the
#     backscatter ratio the scattering-weighted mean, per band. That makes the
#     mixture's properties vary per cell and per layer, which moves the
#     two-stream u-factors from a once-per-call computation outside the level
#     loop to inside it.
#
#  6. A conservative-scattering branch, which is item 5's hazard rather than a
#     refinement. See below.
#
#  7. The longwave sums qlw*od over species in the exponent. Additive already,
#     so N species cost a sum and no restructuring.
#
#  8. The prescribed/interactive exclusion at radini is REMOVED. The two paths
#     were exclusive because they wrote into one slot; the transported tracer is
#     now species ndustrad+1 of the array and they no longer share one. That is
#     what keeps DUST-13 open: while the exclusion stood, choosing interactive
#     dust put sea salt permanently out of the radiation.
#
# THE CONSERVATIVE-SCATTERING BRANCH, AND WHY IT IS NOT OPTIONAL.
# zaeru1 divides by (1 - ssa1). Dust's single-scattering albedo is nowhere near
# 1, so nothing had ever driven that expression toward its limit. Sea salt sits
# at 1 - 1e-5. Measured on the expressions themselves at both precisions:
#
#   8-byte: the exact form holds to 1-ssa = 1e-14; benign.
#   4-byte: at 1-ssa = 1e-8 and below, (1.0 - ssa) rounds to exactly zero and
#           the exact form returns NaN. At 1e-6 it has already drifted past the
#           limit it should approach.
#
# So the failure is an outright NaN in a single-precision build, not the
# plausible wrong number the design note predicted. The threshold is
# SQRT(EPSILON(1.0)), which is where the exact form's error -- machine epsilon
# over (1-ssa), because that difference is formed by subtraction -- crosses the
# limit's error, which goes as (1-ssa) itself. That is 1.5e-8 in 8-byte
# arithmetic and 3.4e-4 in 4-byte, so sea salt takes the exact branch in a
# double build and the limit in a single one, which is right in both.
#
# The limit is the limit of the same expressions, not a different scheme: u*t
# tends to 2*b*tau/mu as ssa goes to 1, so T = 1/(1+b*tau/mu) and
# R = (b*tau/mu)/(1+b*tau/mu). T + R = 1 exactly, so it cannot absorb.
#
# WHY THE knz==1 FAST PATH EXISTS. Where exactly one species is present the
# mixture IS that species, and the code takes its constants directly rather than
# forming (ssa*tau)/tau. That division is not exact in IEEE arithmetic:
# measured, it returns something other than ssa in 12,026 of 100,000 sampled
# cases at 8-byte precision. Without the fast path every single-species cell
# would move by an ulp for no physical reason, and the existing dust-only answer
# would not reproduce.
#
# WHAT IT DOES NOT DO. No species is routed in by this patch. The .sra writer,
# the aerofile column and the config keys for sea salt are CLIM-40, and the
# decision about which aerosols the final climate carries is DUST-13.
#
# WHAT WAS MEASURED, 2026-08-20, T42 L10 on 8 ranks at 8-byte precision.
#
#  REDUCTION IDENTITY. The same configuration -- ndustrad = 1, one prescribed
#  dust column -- through a binary built from the base above and through this
#  one. At ONE timestep the gridpoint output is BIT-IDENTICAL. That is the
#  horizon at which the comparison is valid, and the reason is the next entry.
#
#  THE MODEL IS NOT RUN-TO-RUN REPRODUCIBLE BEYOND A FEW TIMESTEPS. The control
#  that establishes it: the SAME binary, run twice, on the same inputs.
#    1 timestep  -- output bit-identical, so the comparison above means something
#    16 timesteps -- output differs, at byte 40485
#  Old-versus-new at 16 timesteps differs at that same byte 40485, and the
#  difference grows from 2.4e-6 relative in the first differing record to order
#  1 by the end, which is a chaotic amplification of a rounding-level seed and
#  not an effect of this change. Any bit-identity claim about this model has to
#  carry that bound. The restart file plasim_status is worse: it differs between
#  two runs of one binary even at ONE timestep, so it is not a valid comparison
#  target at all.
#
#  COLUMN CONSERVATION, per species, from dustprof's own report against a
#  column maximum of 0.4896:
#    one species   -- max |column - prescribed| = 1.30e-18
#    two species   -- species 1: 8.67e-19, species 2: 0.0 exactly
#  Species 2 was given a 900 m scale height against species 1's 3000 m, and both
#  columns still conserve, which is what the per-species form is for.
#
#  CONSERVATIVE SCATTERING. A second species with Qsca = Qext exactly, so ssa is
#  1 to the bit, ran through the model with no NaN anywhere and T + R - 1 = 0
#  exactly in the branch itself.
#
#  THE MIXING AND THE FAST PATH were measured on the expressions directly, at
#  both precisions, and the numbers are in the note. The one that decides the
#  fast path: (ssa*tau)/tau differs from ssa in 12,026 of 100,000 sampled cases
#  at 8-byte precision.
